@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Task timestamps specification
+
+## Requirement
+
+Record when each task was created and when it was last changed so the app can show task age and recent changes.
+
+## Task schema
+
+Every `Task` has two required readonly fields:
+
+- `createdAt`: ISO-8601 date-time string set when the task is added.
+- `updatedAt`: ISO-8601 date-time string set when the task is added and whenever a task is successfully completed, reopened, renamed, tagged or untagged.
+
+On creation, both fields receive the same timestamp. Failed operations do not change either timestamp. An operation that makes no effective change (same title, duplicate tag, or absent tag) does not count as a task change and leaves `updatedAt` unchanged.
+
+## Clock boundary
+
+The domain list receives a clock function that returns an ISO-8601 date-time string. It calls this function only for successful additions and effective task changes. The public `createTodoList` supplies the current UTC time by default and may receive an alternate clock for deterministic callers and tests. Domain modules do not read the system clock.
+
+## Public API compatibility
+
+Existing list operation arguments remain unchanged. `createTodoList` gains an optional clock function argument. Existing callers therefore continue to work, while callers needing deterministic timestamps can provide a clock.
